  "finalAnswerPreview": "## Verdict\\n\\n**The applicable guarantee is global ordering — one durable, filter‑independent position space shared by all readers of the ledger.** That is Record A. Record B (\\\"per‑consumer\\\") misdescribes the pinned line and is not the governing contract.\\n\\n## What the \\\"integration\\\" is\\n\\nThis workspace is `palimpsest-dsh`, a DSH orchestration plugin that consumes the sister project Ordarium (Safe Action SDK) over a shared local ledger. The only cross‑repo surface here is the pinned `@ordarium/*` dependency line; the ordering question concerns Ordarium's revisioned **state‑change feed** (`StateChangeFeed.changes()` / `StateStore.changes`), the observation capability over the management‑state kind.\\n\\n## The conflict, and why it is resolvable locally\\n\\n`docs/engineering/09-ordering-contract-{a,b}.md` are the only two local statements on this subject, and they contradict each other. Both claim the same scope (\\\"current pinned line\\\", \\\"normative\\\"), carry no dates, no cross‑references, no revision‑log entry, and the archive's precedence rule (archive specs beat user docs) cannot rank two archive records against each other. So doc‑internal provenance alone is silent.\\n\\n**Versio",
